      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The simulated initial material is equiatomic FeCuCrCoNi.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The initial FeCuCrCoNi nanoparticles form a well-mixed solid solution.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Nanoparticles of systematically varied diameter can be subjected to identical controlled temperature ramps in molecular dynamics simulations.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11775865::chunk::000::abstract::cfe160ba3c"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "A heating interval from approximately 298 K to 973 K is suitable for examining the nanoparticle thermal response.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11775865::chunk::000::abstract::cfe160ba3c"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The simulations neglect environmental effects such as oxidation and surface contamination.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Smaller nanoparticles have a greater surface-to-volume ratio.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The greater surface-to-volume ratio of smaller nanoparticles enhances atomic diffusion and surface reordering.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11775865::chunk::000::abstract::cfe160ba3c"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "A larger fraction of surface or near-surface atoms in smaller nanoparticles produces greater atomic mobility.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Greater atomic mobility causes an earlier onset of phase separation or melting.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11775865::chunk::000::abstract::cfe160ba3c"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Larger FeCuCrCoNi nanoparticles behave more like the bulk and therefore have greater thermal stability.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Smaller FeCuCrCoNi nanoparticles will exhibit lower effective melting or structural-transition temperatures than larger nanoparticles.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
